\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.6}{\ignorespaces Offline-buffer fall-through flowchart. The decision tree executed by the Core 0 worker each five-second sample cycle first routes telemetry through the highest-priority online channel. On a non-2xx response, the worker falls through to the next channel; if all channels are exhausted, the record is appended to \texttt  {/tel\_buf.log}. The buffer drains on a five-second cadence with a guaranteed-forward-progress minimum of one record per worker pass.}}{97}{figure.caption.37}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:offline_buffer_fallthrough}{{5.6}{97}{Offline-buffer fall-through flowchart. The decision tree executed by the Core 0 worker each five-second sample cycle first routes telemetry through the highest-priority online channel. On a non-2xx response, the worker falls through to the next channel; if all channels are exhausted, the record is appended to \texttt {/tel\_buf.log}. The buffer drains on a five-second cadence with a guaranteed-forward-progress minimum of one record per worker pass}{figure.caption.37}{}}
